# Interview Arena (LearningArchitect)

Planned showcase module: compact WebGL multiplayer arena for interview preparation.

**Canonical docs:** `UnityClient/Docs/Modules/InterviewArena/`. **Runtime assets & code:** `UnityClient/Assets/Content/Modules/InterviewArena/`.

**Integration:** separate scene (`InterviewArena`) opened from the hub dock — **not** an 8th `ModuleDefinitionSO`. See `UnityClient/Docs/Decisions.md` D-008. Keep `ArchitectureShowcase` as the default build entry (D-001).

**Unity project root:** open `UnityClient/` in Unity Hub. Product docs: `Docs/` at repository root.

## Main intent

- WebGL-first playable slice inside the shared showcase hub
- personal-server lobby flow (mock services in Editor until backend exists)
- physics-based movement, pooling, AI FSM
- clean asmdef split under `Assets/Content/Modules/InterviewArena/`

## Namespaces

Use `LearningArchitect.Modules.InterviewArena.*` (or `InterviewArena.*` only if asmdef root name requires it — keep one convention per folder).

Preferred areas (see `UnityClient/Docs/Modules/InterviewArena/docs/03_UNITY_MODULES.md`):

- Core, Auth, Lobby, Player, Physics, Combat, AI, Multiplayer, UI, Infrastructure

Dependency direction:

```text
UI -> Controllers -> Services -> Infrastructure
Gameplay -> Core/Data
```

## When editing

1. Read `UnityClient/Docs/Modules/InterviewArena/INTEGRATION_ASSESSMENT.md` for phased scope.
2. Match existing showcase patterns in `Assets/Content/Modules/*` and `Assets/Content/Showcase/Runtime`.
3. User-visible strings go to `ShowcaseContent` / `ShowcaseUI`, not variant SO fields.
4. **Do not** runtime-spawn the player with `CreatePrimitive` / `AddComponent` chains. Use prefab + scene references; empty serialized fields are fine until authored.
5. Read `UnityClient/Docs/Modules/InterviewArena/CODE_ARCHITECTURE.md` before adding systems. Prefer NonAlloc physics, input buffering, and `PlayerConfig` tuning.
6. Read `UnityClient/Docs/Modules/InterviewArena/SCENE_COMPOSITION.md` before changing scenes, prefab hierarchy, or UI object names. Runtime pools belong under scene services (`ArenaCombatServices`), not inside actor prefabs. UI widgets use Showcase naming: `Container -`, `Image -`, `Text -`.
